    44	
    45	`_module()` dynamically imports the identity and guard helpers at `exp35_supervisor.py:405-409`. `dry_run()` invokes both at `:816` without setting `sys.dont_write_bytecode`. In a clean writable checkout, those imports may create ignored `__pycache__/*.pyc` files.
    46	
    47	The tests do not observe this: the supervisor is already imported before the snapshot, and `_snapshot` covers only `tmp_path`, not the run worktree (`test_exp35_supervisor_cli.py:19-20,110-119`).
    48	
    49	There is a second dry-run defect: although `:825` reads the current lane from state, `:833-845` always checks GPU 1’s approved tuple and shared predictor. A legitimate resumed GPU-0 state can therefore be falsely refused, while GPU-0 occupancy is not checked as the current lane.
    50	
    51	Concrete fix:
    52	
    53	- Set `sys.dont_write_bytecode = True` before any dynamic import.
    54	- Test the CLI in a fresh committed snapshot with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE` absent and compare the entire snapshot, including ignored files.
    55	- Branch the live check by state lane: exact approved tuple and predictor on shared GPU 1; zero foreign processes and no predictor on GPU 0.
    56	- Enforce the exact two-card map in dry-run as in `Supervisor.tables()`.
    57	
    58	### HIGH 3 — the running-cell watch loses PID-reuse protection
    59	
    60	At `exp35_supervisor.py:608-609`, the approved tuple is reduced to a set of PID numbers. At `:623-626`, any process with an approved PID is exempt without rechecking its start time, cwd, cmdline hash or fd links.
    61	
    62	If the trainer exits and a table job reuses PID 3028196 during a cell, it is not classified as a new process and no stop latch is set. The next pre-spawn identity check prevents another shared spawn, but §13 requires the replacement to latch and be reported after the running cell.
    63	
    64	Concrete fix: while polling, compare every non-descendant process with the complete approved identity. A missing trainer alone may lead to hand-over; an extra or same-PID/different-identity process must latch. Add an in-flight PID-reuse test.
